name w2-10-opera
timeout 900
time 1981-06-07T12:55:00Z

# CAMPAIGN W2, SORTIE 10 OF 10 - OSIRAK 1981 (OPERATION OPERA): REACH, NOT COMBAT.
# THE FULL RAID. THE ONE NUMBER THE CAMPAIGN EXISTS TO PRODUCE: BOMBS ON TARGET x AIRCRAFT RECOVERED.
# Spec, anchor and sources: doc/campaigns/w2-osirak.md. Format: doc/missions/campaign.md.
# CONTROL: none, and it has no sibling. IT IS THE TERMINUS OF THE CAMPAIGN'S ONE CHAIN: w2-06 -> w2-10
# carries `w2esc1`/`w2esc2` with whatever the escort sortie left them - the aircraft if it survived,
# and the rounds it did not shoot. This sortie is also run STANDALONE outside the ten so the carry is
# a number rather than a claim (campaign file §State).
#
# THE ANCHOR: eight F-16A and six F-15A, launched 15:55 local on 7 June 1981, over 1,600 km round
# trip, ingress at 30 m [T4] or 240 m [T4] ([DISPUTED], see w2-02), external tanks exhausted en route
# and jettisoned over the Saudi desert, pop-up to 2,100 m at 20 km, 35 deg dive at 1,100 km/h,
# release at 1,100 m in pairs 5 seconds apart, under 2 minutes over the target, sixteen Mk-84 released
# of which "at least eight" struck the dome, AAA the only defence met, NO LOSSES [T4].
#
# WHAT THIS FILE REPRODUCES AND WHAT IT CANNOT, ITEM BY ITEM, BEFORE ANY RESULT IS READ:
#   package size 8 + escort        REPRODUCED - eight strikers in four pairs plus two escorts
#   the escort's TYPE              NOT reproduced (`C7`): two F-16 stand in for six F-15A, and only
#                                  two of them, because the anchor's other four were a dispersed
#                                  diversion with no geometry this file could give them
#   the 1,600 km round trip        NOT FLOWN, AND THE REASON IS TWO-PART. (a) O1's rule: two
#                                  engagements in one file must be separated in TIME, because
#                                  `FirstFlightKo` ends the whole run at the first flight-monitor K.O.
#                                  - so the strike has to be complete before the escort's merge, which
#                                  bounds the ingress. (b) a nine-run determinism sweep over a
#                                  1,966 km capstone with twelve aircraft is hours of wall clock for
#                                  no extra information, because THE RANGE IS MEASURED WHERE IT IS
#                                  CHEAP: sorties 03/04/05 and the flameout ladder. This file flies
#                                  the LAST 60 km of the ingress, and 60 was MEASURED rather than
#                                  chosen: at 150 km the scramble killed the escort lead at
#                                  t = 664.7 s with the package still 12 km short of the dome and
#                                  `FirstFlightKo` ended the run there. At 60 km the release falls at
#                                  ~292 s and the merge at ~515 s, in that order
#   the fuel state at that point   DERIVED, NOT CHOSEN. The war-load flameout probe (2 x Mk-84 +
#                                  2 x tank370, 240 m, 400 kt) is read at 922.9 km from Etzion, which
#                                  is 982.9 - 60: fuelLbs = 5,340.6 of the model's own 6,972.0 lb
#                                  internal capacity -> `set fuel_int_pct 76.60` [DERIVED]
#   the tanks jettisoned en route  DECLARED AS A STATE, NOT FLOWN, AND THE PRICE IS NAMED. The
#                                  externals run dry at 675.8 km on that configuration [MEASURED] and
#                                  the anchor drops them there. FlightBox CANNOT: `FBStoresSystem`
#                                  releases in STATION ORDER, so a jettison on a jet carrying Mk-84 on
#                                  stations 3 and 7 drops a BOMB first (MEASURED, the jettison probe:
#                                  `sms RELEASE station=3 store=mk84` at t=3295.6 before
#                                  `TANK_JETTISON station=4` at t=3300.6). Selective jettison is named
#                                  as a simplification in doc/modules/stores.md §Gaps and this is the
#                                  file where it bites. The strikers therefore spawn CLEAN of tanks
#                                  with the derived internal fuel above
#   16 bombs                       NOT REPRODUCIBLE: `FBPilot`'s attack phase pickles ONCE per pass
#                                  and there is no re-attack (doc/pilot.md §2.11), so eight aircraft
#                                  release EIGHT Mk-84. The second bomb on each jet stays on the rail
#                                  and is carried out by the campaign layer's `stores` fact
#   pairs 5 seconds apart          AUTHORED, NOT COMPUTED (`C15`, no time-on-target). The four pairs
#                                  are spaced 1,029 m along track = 5.00 s at the commanded 400 kt /
#                                  205.8 m/s [DERIVED]. THAT IS WHAT `C15` MEANS: the arithmetic is in
#                                  this comment instead of in the simulator, and nothing keeps the
#                                  spacing if anything perturbs it. This is the slot of the spec's
#                                  dropped mission 5 (`w2-05-pair-pop`) - see the campaign header
#   pop-up, 35 deg dive, 1,100 m   NOT REPRODUCIBLE (`C10`): every release below is a LEVEL laydown at
#                                  240 m. w2-01 measured what that is worth against `target_hard`
#   under 2 minutes over target    a CONSEQUENCE here, not a declaration: read the first and last
#                                  `stores SEPARATION` ticks
#   AAA as the only defence        REPRODUCED - four guns on the site, as in w2-08
#   the late scramble              REPRODUCED IN SHAPE: two MiG-29 inbound from 250 km beyond the site,
#                                  which is what makes their merge fall AFTER the strike (O1's rule)
#   no losses                      that is the anchor's RESULT, not its setup, and it is what this
#                                  sortie is scored against
#
# THE ONE TACTICAL QUESTION: WITH EIGHT AIRCRAFT, ONE AIM POINT AND NO TANKER, DOES THE PACKAGE GET
# HOME? Two integers: bombs inside the dome's 17.7 m fail radius (derived in w2-01), and aircraft that
# end the run alive with fuel left.
#
# THE AIR HALF OF THIS SORTIE IS DECLARED OUTCOME-BLIND, IN ADVANCE. W1 put a campaign's own ten
# missions through the saturation gate on 2026-07-30 and the gate REFUSED the arena: only the rungs at
# 1v1 and 2v1 decided anything, so AN AIR-TO-AIR RESULT ABOVE TWO AIRCRAFT A SIDE IS A FIXED POINT IN
# THIS TREE. This capstone is 10 v 2 in the air. ITS AIR RESULT DOES NOT GRADE and nothing in the
# campaign's conclusion rests on it; the gradeable air measurement is w2-06, which is 2 v 1 on purpose.
# WHAT DOES GRADE HERE is the ground half and the fuel half, which is exactly what W1 measured about
# every other capstone in this directory.
#
# THE ARENA: the last 150 km of the raid's inbound track, bearing 068.37 deg, into Al-Tuwaitha.
#   `w2dom0` target_hard  33.20000 44.52000 - the reactor containment dome, THE aim point of all eight
#   the package spawns 60.0-63.1 km short of it and egresses 80 km back down the inbound track
#   `w2sit1` target_soft  33.20026 44.52080 -  80 m along track
#   `w2sit2` target_soft  33.19866 44.52063 - 160 m across track
#   `w2sit3` target_soft  33.19960 44.51880 - 120 m back along track
#   `w2sit4` target_soft  33.20167 44.51921 - 200 m across the other way
#   `w2flk0` zsu23 33.19172 44.49505 / `w2flk9` zu23 33.21670 44.51208 - the site's guns
#   `w2mig1`/`w2mig2` mig29 34.02782 47.02681 - scrambled, 250 km beyond the site
#
# THE SIX STRUCTURAL DISCLOSURES, in short form (full text in w2-01-dome.fbm): `C5` half closed - the
# tank exists, AERIAL REFUELLING DOES NOT, and this file's whole fuel state is a consequence of that;
# `C20` open, `--elev const`, 0 m plane, real ground under this route 42.83-1,599.22 m (MEASURED);
# `C10` level laydown; `C7` no F-15; `FirstFlightKo` handled by the time split above; W1's fixed point
# declared above. Fuel discipline: `set fuel_int_pct`, never `set fuel_pct`.
#
# READING RULE (binding): the exit code is NOT the verdict of this sortie. Read, in this order:
# (1) how many of the eight reached release and what each `stores DELIVERY aimErrM` was, against the
# 17.7 m the dome needs, (2) the dome's and the four buildings' `UNIT_RESULT`, (3) how many aircraft
# are alive at the end and what `fuelLbs` each has left, (4) the two guns' engagement lines, (5)
# `campaign ATTRITION` / `campaign EXPENDED` and the `campaign CARRY` lines the escort brought in.
# Do NOT read the air-to-air outcome as a result at all - the paragraph above says why.

# MEASURED (fingerprint 660805cbd5aa3b1b, exit 1): EIGHT BOMBS, FIVE INSIDE THE LETHAL RADIUS, THE
# DOME DOWN, EIGHT STRIKERS BACK, THE ESCORT LOST.
#   the releases  8 of 8, at t=290.8 / 295.8 / 300.8 / 305.9 s by pair. THE AUTHORED 1,029 m SPACING
#                 COMES OUT AT 5.00 s, FOUR TIMES, TO THE TICK - which is what `C15` means: it works,
#                 and nothing in the simulator maintains it
#   the errors    `aimErrM` 6.42 / 7.02 / 6.78 / 7.34 / 6.36 / 26.32 / 26.23 / 26.67 m. FIVE OF EIGHT
#                 INSIDE THE DOME'S 17.7 m FAIL RADIUS (derived in w2-01). `aimAcrossM` -1.29 to
#                 -1.44 m on all eight: the error is along track, as everywhere in this tree
#   the ground    `w2dom0` DESTROYED by 8 hits, `w2sit1` (80 m) with it; `w2sit2`/`w2sit3`/`w2sit4`
#                 INTACT. Bombs on target x aircraft recovered = 8 x 8
#   time on tgt   first to last separation 15.1 s, against the anchor's "under 2 minutes"
#   the fuel      all eight spawn at 5,340.4 lb (the derived post-922.9 km state) and end at
#                 4,675-4,677 lb; the escort the same
#   the loss      the scramble arrives after the strike, by construction: the escort is killed at
#                 t=515-518 s, 210 s after the last bomb. The run ends there (`FirstFlightKo`)
#   THE CARRY (attribution A5, this file run STANDALONE): one `campaign CARRY unit=w2esc1 action=drop
#                 reason="destroyed in an earlier mission"`. Standalone the escort element ends 1 OF 2
#                 ALIVE - `w2esc1` killed at t=515.1, `w2esc2` alive. In campaign it ends 0 OF 1:
#                 `w2esc1` never takes off and `w2esc2` is killed at t=517.6. REMOVING THE AIRCRAFT
#                 THAT WOULD HAVE DIED KILLS THE ONE THAT WOULD HAVE LIVED. Depth: 8 of 29 common
#                 telemetry files byte-identical, and the eight are EXACTLY THE EIGHT BOMBS. Every
#                 aircraft file moved; not one bomb file did. The carry moves the air half and not one
#                 metre of the strike

unit w2op11
  module f16
  team friendly
  flight ope1 1
  spawn 33.00758 43.91894 240 68.4 400        # pair 1, left. 60.000 km short of the dome
  set gear up
  set fuel_int_pct 76.60                      # 5,340.6 lb - the derived state after 922.9 km
  set datalink on
  set fcr_mode off
  set rwr on
  set store 3 mk84
  set store 7 mk84
  set cmds_mode auto
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set cmds_flare 60
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task attack
  set attack_mode ccrp
  wp 33.20000 44.52000 240 400
  wp 32.93511 43.72283 240 400
  objective kill unit w2dom0
  objective survive

